WEBVTT

00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:04.470
It's raining again today...

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:07.270
It's getting to be a bit depressing.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:10.500
It has been raining all the time lately.

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:13.720
By the way, where is Hanako-san?

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:16.120
I wonder what happened to her.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:21.220
<b>June 27</b>

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.220
Good morning.

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:23.530
Good morning.

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:27.980
Let's see... Hanakoizumi-san still isn't here?

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:29.740
How unusual.

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:37.230
Now, your new happiness training
assignment for today will be

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:38.970
"making your wishes come true."

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:41.940
Huh? Wishes?

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:45.310
Do you have any wishes you 
would like to have come true?

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:46.640
Wishes?

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:48.560
To begin with, wishes are—

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:53.820
Good morning.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:58.910
Goodness, Hanakoizumi-san, 
what happened? You're a mess.

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:00.540
I'm sorry.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:04.680
When I left home this morning, 
a ton of cats rained on me.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:06.600
Then my umbrella meowed and ran away.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.750
Then I fell into the river, 
and it just kept raining, and then...

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:14.920
I see. Honestly, I don't know 
what you're talking about,

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:17.010
but I can see that you had a rough morning.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.970
Do you have a towel?

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:21.110
Yep!

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:24.860
Huh? It's soaked.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.620
Teacher, I have one.

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:27.260
Then help her dry off, please.

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:28.200
That's odd... Huh?

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:31.150
In the meantime, I'll hand out what 
you'll need for your assignment.

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:37.880
Are you okay?

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:41.270
Yeah, I'm fine. Thanks.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:46.800
My body feels kinda floaty...

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:51.120
Hanako-san, what happened to 
the hair barrette you usually wear?

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:54.970
It came off on the way here.

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:57.550
The clip seems to be broken.

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:00.120
What's that sound?

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:05.760
Hanako, are you okay?

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:06.940
Hanako-san!

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:43.490
Making our wishes come true...

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:45.990
Another ridiculous assignment.

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:48.790
And I can't believe she gave us these

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:51.000
for the Star Festival.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.000
I know.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:57.280
It's presumptuous enough just 
for me to wish for anything.

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:00.840
Regardless, there's no way wishes 
can come true that easily.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:04.240
This one is...

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:05.760
Hanako-san's.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:11.830
I'm a bit worried that our normally 
energetic Hanako-san went home early.

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:17.730
Me, too.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.300
And then there's this.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:23.870
Why don't we take this
and her paper strip to her?

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:29.490
Yes, let's go check on her and take
her something she might like.

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:33.250
<b>Episode 7</b>

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:33.250
<b>June 28</b>

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:33.250
<b>Visiting Hanako</b>

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:41.450
We can't bring any dogs or cats with us.

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:45.010
That's right. I wonder what 
else Hanako-san would like.

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:47.970
Hanako seems to be the most happy...

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:57.100
Go! Attack!

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.090
Forward! Forward!

00:04:58.090 --> 00:04:59.260
...all the time.

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:03.580
Hanako-san is always smiling.

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:07.520
Let's try looking for things 
we would be happy to get.

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:08.280
Okay.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.760
Vr-vr-vroom, vr-vr-vroom!

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:15.250
How about this?

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:16.960
<b>Snake Power</b>

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:19.170
The eight-headed snake?

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:22.830
I did say things we'd like, but...

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:24.510
You don't think she'd like it?

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:25.630
Probably not.

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:28.390
Then I'll get this for myself.

00:05:28.670 --> 00:05:30.520
This should hold me for three days.

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:31.390
Three days...

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:33.540
What else is there?

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:37.450
This is...

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:46.280
Um... I don't think it would 
suit me, but maybe Hanako...

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:49.770
No, I'm sure it would look good on you, too.

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:51.160
N-No way...

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:53.620
In contrast,

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:55.340
if I were to wear it,

00:05:55.340 --> 00:06:02.220
I'm sure the cute ribbons and lace 
would appear monstrously hideous.

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:04.590
I don't think that's true.

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:06.550
I bought it.

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:13.000
We didn't find anything...

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:15.930
Thank you!

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:19.850
<b>Strawberry Milk</b>

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:21.920
I'd like a ginseng milk with grated yam, please.

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:22.860
Is that good?

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:24.890
Thank you!

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:28.030
Okay, we've got our gifts. Let's hurry.

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:32.810
Yeah. Hanako-san's house is 
just past this arcade ahead...

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:38.070
Was it raining this hard before?

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:49.340
Hanakoizumi

00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:51.720
This is Hanako's house, right?

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:54.290
Yes, it seems that way.

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:59.560
For some reason, I'm getting an
overwhelmingly negative vibe from it...

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:03.020
I-I'm not scared.

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:06.040
Yes?

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:08.790
Who might you be?

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:10.760
Oh, those uniforms...

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:15.800
Y-Yes, I'm Hibarigaoka Ruri of 
Tennomifune Academy, Class 1-7.

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:18.440
My name is Kumegawa Botan.

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:20.370
Um, today Hanako-san went home—

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:23.630
Excuse us for a minute.

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:28.040
What was Hanako's real name again?

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:29.640
Um...

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:33.790
You must be Anne's friends, 
Hibari-san and Botan-san.

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:34.680
Anne!

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:35.560
Yes!

00:07:37.030 --> 00:07:41.600
She's been talking about 
you two all the time lately.

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:44.610
Um, are you Anne-san's sister?

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:46.490
Sister?

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:52.940
I'm Anne's mother.

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:56.070
<b>Hanakoizumi
Sakura</b>

00:07:52.940 --> 00:07:56.070
There's no need to talk out here. Please, come in.

00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:02.160
Anne! Anne, are you awake?

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:04.670
Your friends are here.

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:08.250
Actually, if you could just 
give this to Anne-san...

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:10.830
Hibari-chan and Botan-chan!

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:11.880
You came!

00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:15.790
Goodness.

00:08:15.790 --> 00:08:16.850
A-Are you okay?

00:08:17.150 --> 00:08:19.560
Why is there a cushion here?

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:24.730
She's always been scatterbrained, 
and she trips all the time,

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:27.720
so I've taken appropriate 
measures in danger zones.

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:32.210
Anne, are you okay?

00:08:32.210 --> 00:08:33.950
I don't know who you take after.

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:35.860
<b>Konk</b>

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:38.480
It's genetic.

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:39.950
It certainly is.

00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:41.500
Gifts!

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:42.960
Yes, gifts!

00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:46.120
It's delicious!

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:49.870
Sorry for creating such a commotion, Hanako.

00:08:49.870 --> 00:08:53.100
No, I'm really happy you came.

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:55.600
I'm glad you seem to be feeling better.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:57.450
My fever's already down.

00:08:57.450 --> 00:08:59.640
Sorry for scaring you this morning.

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:03.310
Would you like some tea?

00:09:06.550 --> 00:09:10.940
Seeing those uniforms makes me feel
like my friends have come to visit.

00:09:11.590 --> 00:09:15.490
My mom was a student at 
Tennomifune Academy, too.

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:17.420
Really?

00:09:17.420 --> 00:09:19.420
Were you in class...

00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:20.370
Class 7.

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:23.580
<b>Class 7 =
Happiness Class</b>

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:21.880
I knew it.

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:23.580
Of course.

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:26.110
Just like us.

00:09:26.110 --> 00:09:28.290
Yes, lucky seven!

00:09:29.490 --> 00:09:34.350
By the way, I hope my daughter 
isn't causing you any trouble.

00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:36.570
What? Trouble?

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:39.580
After all, she's so clumsy.

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:41.790
No, not at all.

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:44.390
Oh, right! Speaking of clumsy...

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:48.700
I'm so clumsy!

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:52.270
Oh, my...

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:52.270
This is...

00:09:54.020 --> 00:09:55.290
And this one!

00:09:55.740 --> 00:10:00.760
Animals always attacked her 
when I tried to take her picture,

00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:05.450
but I'm glad she was able to attend 
her entrance ceremonies.

00:10:05.740 --> 00:10:07.060
Yeah...

00:10:08.740 --> 00:10:11.070
Oh! I'm sorry.

00:10:11.070 --> 00:10:13.380
I only meant to bring tea.

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:15.260
Take your time.

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:17.100
Thanks!

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:21.180
Your mom is a lot like you.

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:23.790
She's such a fun mother.

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:26.750
Anyway...

00:10:27.550 --> 00:10:31.720
Hanako-san, you look so different
with your hair down.

00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:33.100
You think so?

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:37.860
I usually tie the long parts 
on the sides into a bun.

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:40.490
That's one way to do it...

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:42.670
Hibari-san, are you interested 
in her hairstyle?

00:10:42.670 --> 00:10:46.380
I-It's not like I'm interested 
in cute hairstyles or anything!

00:10:47.150 --> 00:10:50.330
Besides, cute doesn't suit me.

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:56.550
You never know until you try!

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:56.550
Hey, wait!

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:03.760
So cute!

00:11:04.550 --> 00:11:08.250
Hibari-san, you look absolutely adorable!

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:11.140
Your dark, silky hair is so beautiful.

00:11:11.510 --> 00:11:14.910
Compared to my naturally curly, dull hair,

00:11:14.910 --> 00:11:17.460
it's like the difference between 
the moon and a rat.

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:20.250
Naturally curly hair is cute too, Botan-chan!

00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:22.940
The only people who ever say that

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:27.010
Heh Heh Heh

00:11:22.940 --> 00:11:25.800
are people who don't have 
naturally curly hair.

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:33.100
But I think your loose 
braids look good on you.

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:35.640
I'd like to see you with 
your hair down, though.

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:36.860
Yeah.

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:40.510
Huh? What's going on?

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:44.680
D-Don't!

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:46.300
I-I can't...

00:11:50.530 --> 00:11:52.200
M-My glasses...

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:56.010
O-Oh, no!

00:11:56.010 --> 00:11:58.940
I can't redo my own hair 
once it comes undone,

00:11:58.940 --> 00:12:01.570
and I can't see anything without my glasses!

00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:02.480
My head...

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:04.070
She's as unfortunate as she is beautiful...

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:09.770
Hanako-san, you should try 
a different hairstyle, too.

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:10.790
Botan-chan?

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:14.290
Sounds
like fun!

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:13.830
Are they play-wrestling?

00:12:17.890 --> 00:12:19.840
Come on, cut it out.

00:12:20.730 --> 00:12:22.840
P-Please, no more...

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:24.890
Okay, next...

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:26.510
It's your turn, Hanako-san.

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:27.660
We're still going?

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:30.090
Of course. This way, please.

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:30.970
Let's do it!

00:12:31.320 --> 00:12:33.100
Oh, gosh, look at the time.

00:12:33.760 --> 00:12:35.260
You're right.

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:40.300
Sorry, we meant to leave right away.

00:12:40.300 --> 00:12:44.680
It's okay. I feel a lot better 
after talking to you two.

00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:47.950
You really do look better.

00:12:48.270 --> 00:12:49.830
Oh, right. Here.

00:12:50.110 --> 00:12:52.250
Oh, thanks!

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:55.640
My mom gave me this. 
It's really special to me.

00:12:57.220 --> 00:12:59.020
Well, we should get going.

00:12:59.020 --> 00:12:59.760
Okay.

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:02.840
See you tomorrow, Hibari-chan and Botan-chan.

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:06.150
Go... home!

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:08.330
Thanks for having us.

00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:10.040
Sorry we stayed so late.

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:12.770
Not at all. Come back soon.

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:14.750
Hanakoizumi

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:23.240
I just felt a chill...

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:27.060
What is this sinister feeling?

00:13:33.970 --> 00:13:36.460
<b>June 28</b>

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:43.840
I can't believe she's out again today.

00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:47.320
We should've left earlier yesterday.

00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:48.300
Yes...

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:52.820
As for me, even though 
I had joint pain last night

00:13:52.820 --> 00:13:57.040
followed by a migraine setting in 
around two in the morning,

00:13:57.040 --> 00:14:03.290
I felt completely better in the 
morning and dared to come to school.

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:10.650
The rain's not letting up.

00:14:12.800 --> 00:14:14.400
Now my stomach hurts...

00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:15.330
Huh?!

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:24.750
I wanted to go to school.

00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:39.740
It's quiet without her here.

00:14:39.740 --> 00:14:42.990
Hanakoizumi-san is absent again today, I see.

00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:45.750
Yes, it seems she has a fever.

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:48.910
She got rained on again yesterday.

00:14:48.910 --> 00:14:49.800
The rain...

00:14:58.970 --> 00:15:03.950
It was raining exceptionally hard 
around Hanako's house yesterday.

00:15:03.950 --> 00:15:05.880
The sky was pitch black, too.

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:09.590
If only the rain would stop...

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:13.770
May I?

00:15:13.770 --> 00:15:15.530
Yes, of course.

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:23.230
Is that...

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:25.320
A teru teru bozu?

00:15:30.600 --> 00:15:31.310
Done.

00:15:31.310 --> 00:15:33.130
It's not supposed to be asleep!

00:15:33.130 --> 00:15:33.930
Really?

00:15:36.020 --> 00:15:39.070
Yeah, that doesn't seem like it 
would make the rain stop.

00:15:39.070 --> 00:15:42.410
This always happens when 
I let Ren handle things!

00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:46.090
Lunchtime is over.

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:48.360
Our next class is...

00:15:48.360 --> 00:15:49.450
Music!

00:15:49.450 --> 00:15:52.050
Hurry to the music room, please.

00:15:50.480 --> 00:15:51.640
Whoops!

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:54.360
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

00:15:55.510 --> 00:15:57.160
Hurry!

00:15:57.160 --> 00:15:58.110
Again?

00:16:01.590 --> 00:16:04.730
If I stick this part here...

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:09.680
Bamboo, bamboo!

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:11.110
Let's hurry along.

00:16:16.550 --> 00:16:18.540
Okay, let's get started.

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:20.750
What's that?

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:23.320
Hibiki's art kit.

00:16:23.320 --> 00:16:25.460
She's been using it since kindergarten.

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:28.940
There's no telling when 
inspiration will strike,

00:16:28.940 --> 00:16:30.670
so I always carry it around with me.

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:32.920
I do something similar.

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:34.680
What's that?

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:36.890
It's my first aid kit.

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:39.680
You do always have it with you.

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:42.060
You're going to use that 
to make a teru teru bozu?

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:43.020
Yes.

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:44.960
I feel like I can make something decent

00:16:44.960 --> 00:16:47.600
with the bandages I'm accustomed to using.

00:16:49.100 --> 00:16:50.260
I'll use...

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:55.920
That's the handkerchief you 
use to wrap your lunches.

00:16:55.920 --> 00:16:57.530
Yeah, that's right.

00:16:58.240 --> 00:16:59.790
It's so plain.

00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:00.860
Of course it is!

00:17:00.860 --> 00:17:02.230
Normal is best.

00:17:04.130 --> 00:17:05.440
Some time later...

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:12.170
Evil rain, grovel before my great might.

00:17:13.940 --> 00:17:15.610
Be gentle.

00:17:16.710 --> 00:17:20.090
I had these bandages specially ordered.

00:17:20.090 --> 00:17:24.140
They're gentle on cuts and 
flexible enough to move with you.

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:28.100
<b>Heh 
Heh
Heh</b>

00:17:24.620 --> 00:17:26.990
My bandages...

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:28.100
That has nothing to do with teru teru bozu...

00:17:28.600 --> 00:17:30.820
You can use this as an example.

00:17:30.820 --> 00:17:32.070
Yeah, right!

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:33.150
Hey, hey.

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:35.740
Spinny, spinny, leap!

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:38.110
What are you girls doing?

00:17:38.110 --> 00:17:40.150
Oh, it's you.

00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:49.790
You don't react much to me when 
Hanakoizumi-san isn't here.

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:52.860
We were hoping Hanako would show up.

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:55.800
That's why we're making teru teru bozu.

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:56.900
I see!

00:17:56.900 --> 00:17:59.190
Timo, Timo, Timo!

00:17:59.190 --> 00:18:01.530
If there's anything I can do, let me know.

00:18:01.530 --> 00:18:03.470
I'll do any... thing...

00:18:03.780 --> 00:18:08.570
<i>Stare...</i>

00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:09.650
What?

00:18:11.560 --> 00:18:12.250
Yeah.

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:14.900
Huh? What?

00:18:15.560 --> 00:18:17.040
Good things come to those who wait.

00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:18.610
It's done!

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:24.520
Is that a teru teru bozu?

00:18:24.520 --> 00:18:27.530
It obviously is, no matter how you look at it.

00:18:27.530 --> 00:18:31.540
Do you not understand its sublime appearance?

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:33.250
Mine is finished, too.

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:35.090
Yours, too?!

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:37.960
Mine is clearly better.

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:39.510
Neither is very good.

00:18:41.860 --> 00:18:42.970
I'm finished, too.

00:18:43.280 --> 00:18:44.640
That's...

00:18:45.030 --> 00:18:46.910
A Hanako teru teru bozu.

00:18:46.910 --> 00:18:50.400
It's smiling just like Hanako-san.

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:53.590
But if you name it after her,

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:57.390
it seems even more unlikely
that the rain will ever stop.

00:18:57.390 --> 00:18:58.400
Ren, how about you?

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:00.110
I'm finished.

00:19:05.670 --> 00:19:07.430
Stay like this until morning.

00:19:07.430 --> 00:19:08.290
Seriously?

00:19:08.590 --> 00:19:09.360
Seriously.

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:12.520
Well, I did say I'd do anything.

00:19:12.520 --> 00:19:14.170
You can do it. I know you can.

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:14.710
Sure.

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:21.860
Pork cutlet bowl...

00:19:24.770 --> 00:19:26.310
My, this is...

00:20:31.540 --> 00:20:33.750
All right! I'm first today!

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:35.210
Good morning.

00:20:36.160 --> 00:20:37.590
I'm not first?!

00:20:38.040 --> 00:20:39.760
You're awfully early.

00:20:39.760 --> 00:20:44.030
Hibiki wanted to come early 
to check on the teru teru bozu.

00:20:44.030 --> 00:20:45.350
Don't tell them that, Ren!

00:20:46.150 --> 00:20:48.300
I'm glad the sky cleared up.

00:20:49.490 --> 00:20:51.960
I'd like three more pork cutlet bowls, please.

00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:54.020
Also one tempura bowl, one beef bowl,

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:57.420
one chicken and egg bowl, one wall slam...

00:20:55.270 --> 00:20:56.480
Good work.

00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:05.690
Do you think Hanako will come?

00:21:05.690 --> 00:21:06.650
She will.

00:21:06.650 --> 00:21:08.920
Yeah, of course she'll come.

00:21:08.920 --> 00:21:09.690
Yeah.

00:21:21.300 --> 00:21:22.230
Huh?

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:26.410
Good morning! You're all so early!

00:21:26.410 --> 00:21:27.360
Hanako!

00:21:27.360 --> 00:21:29.040
Is your fever gone?

00:21:29.040 --> 00:21:31.220
Yeah. I'm all better now.

00:21:31.220 --> 00:21:35.180
And since it's so nice outside, I felt 
so good that I came to school early.

00:21:36.500 --> 00:21:37.850
Of course you did!

00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:39.690
Hibiki-chan, what's that?

00:21:41.280 --> 00:21:42.320
The rain let up because—

00:21:42.320 --> 00:21:44.030
<b>Whack</b>

00:21:44.920 --> 00:21:46.850
What'd you do that for, Ren?

00:21:46.850 --> 00:21:48.700
Hibiki, shut up.

00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:50.450
H-Hanako, your hairstyle...

00:21:50.450 --> 00:21:53.700
Yeah! My mom fixed it for me!

00:21:55.060 --> 00:22:01.450
Your usual hairstyle with that barrette 
might be your best look after all.

00:22:03.350 --> 00:22:04.080
Huh?

00:22:04.420 --> 00:22:08.180
Hibari-chan, that teru teru bozu is so cute!

00:22:08.490 --> 00:22:09.530
Thanks.

00:22:10.730 --> 00:22:12.250
Good morning.

00:22:13.700 --> 00:22:17.150
Are you feeling better, Hanakoizumi-san?

00:22:17.150 --> 00:22:18.010
Yep!

00:22:18.010 --> 00:22:19.940
That's good to hear.

00:22:20.550 --> 00:22:23.930
By the way, were you all able 
to complete your assignment?

00:22:23.930 --> 00:22:25.140
Assignment?

00:22:26.160 --> 00:22:30.370
Your wishes for happiness 
training are due today.

00:22:33.220 --> 00:22:34.290
What's wrong?

00:22:34.640 --> 00:22:37.290
We forgot about the assignment.

00:22:40.060 --> 00:22:41.920
Oh, but did you?

00:22:42.300 --> 00:22:43.130
Huh?

00:22:43.130 --> 00:22:45.650
The paper strips are only extras.

00:22:45.650 --> 00:22:49.180
The assignment was simply 
to make your wishes come true.

00:22:50.000 --> 00:22:52.160
No matter how small a wish is,

00:22:52.160 --> 00:22:54.300
if all you do is wait for it to come true,

00:22:54.300 --> 00:22:55.560
nothing will change.

00:22:56.040 --> 00:22:59.920
You need to take the first step 
toward making your wish come true.

00:22:59.920 --> 00:23:04.480
That is the key to someday 
achieving happiness.

00:23:04.760 --> 00:23:09.780
And if that's the case, then isn't 
it already within your reach?

00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:14.360
I wrote mine!

00:23:15.430 --> 00:23:18.200
Shall we go outside, then?

00:23:18.560 --> 00:23:19.850
Yeah!

00:23:27.570 --> 00:23:33.780
The strawberry milk was delicious!
-Hanako

00:23:34.950 --> 00:23:39.960
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:34.950 --> 00:23:39.960
<b>July 11</b>

00:23:34.950 --> 00:23:39.960
<b>Fighting Final Exams</b>

00:23:39.960 --> 00:23:42.940
<b>Don't miss the next episode!</b>
